Loaded these 3 tools. Call them directly from now on, with input that matches the input_schema:
{"name":"preview_start","description":"To check a change on the running app, start the project's dev server from its launch file (.claude/launch.json or .g-code/launch.json), or reuse it if it already runs. The command runs in the background like bash with run_in_background, under the same approval, and this call waits up to 60s for its port to answer. Returns the URL to open with the browser tools; preview_logs reads the server's errors, and preview_stop stops it. Without a launch file it explains how to write one.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The launch entry's name, such as \"web\"; omit it when the launch file has one entry."}},"additionalProperties":false}}
{"name":"preview_stop","description":"Stop a dev server this session started with preview_start: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL a few seconds later. Servers Geno did not start are never stopped.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The launch entry's name, of a server preview_start started."}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}}
{"name":"preview_logs","description":"Read a dev server's stdout and stderr: its last lines, or only the lines at a level or containing a search text. level \"error\" keeps lines that mention an error, exception, failure or fatal; \"warn\" adds warnings. Secrets are replaced with [redacted]. It only reads.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The launch entry's name, of a server preview_start started; omit it when this session started one."},"level":{"type":"string","enum":["all","warn","error"],"description":"Which lines to keep. Defaults to all."},"search":{"type":"string","description":"Keep only lines that contain this text, ignoring case."},"lines":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":500,"description":"How many of the newest matching lines to return. Defaults to 50."}},"additionalProperties":false}}

This workspace has no launch file: neither .g-code/launch.json nor .claude/launch.json exists. Create .claude/launch.json with edit (create: true), then call preview_start again. For example:
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "dev",
      "runtimeExecutable": "npm",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "run",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 3000
    }
  ]
}
name is what preview_start takes. runtimeExecutable and runtimeArgs are the command, run from the workspace root, or from cwd, a workspace-relative folder, when given. port is where it listens; 3000 is Next.js's default, so check the dev script and the project's config. url is optional and defaults to http://localhost:<port>; it must be on this machine.
